            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"Carmen\"</strong><br>\nBizet's best-known work is the opera \"Carmen,\" which premiered in 1875. It was initially met with shock and distaste because of its break from traditional opera and its portrayal of sexuality and violence. However, \"Carmen\" eventually won acclaim and is now one of the most frequently performed operas worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nBizet married Geneviève Halévy in 1869. They had one son, but Bizet's constant work and health issues often strained the family. He was known to be a passionate and sensitive individual, which was reflected in the emotional depth of his compositions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Works and Untimely Death</strong><br>\nMany of Bizet's later works were not recognized until after his death. He died suddenly of a heart attack at the age of 36, just three months after the premiere of \"Carmen.\" His death was seen as a significant loss to French musical theatre.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
