          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nAfter Bizet's death, his works gained recognition and were praised for their originality and brilliance. \"Carmen,\" in particular, was celebrated for its vivid characters and its blending of the dramatic narrative with melodic music.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nBizet's influence on the development of opera and his role in establishing new directions for French music have been significant. His work paved the way for later operatic composers, who were inspired by his incorporation of realism and his strong characterizations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Remembering Bizet</strong><br>\nToday, Georges Bizet is remembered as a pioneering figure in music who pushed the boundaries of operatic storytelling. His compositions continue to be celebrated for their emotional power and their innovative contributions to the musical world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
